  "id": "immunocytochemistry",
  "term": "immunocytochemistry",
  "definition": "Immunocytochemistry is a laboratory method used to find specific proteins or antigens in cells placed on slides, including cells grown in a single layer or in suspension. It uses antibodies or other target-binding molecules that are made visible by a chemical reaction.",
